# The Color picker, on the four platforms that have it. The tour ends at the
# Options screen; this scene walks the one setting the black-and-white
# platforms do not offer: aplite has no settings windows at all, and diorite
# has them but no colour, so Color is in neither's enum. It opens the picker at
# its shipped default, picks a swatch, and shows the whole app recoloured.
#
# Shot names are prefixed with the scene's own step counter, which restarts at
# 01, so they are given distinct names (color-*) and copied from the scene's
# tmp output into the platform folder beside the tour's files without
# collision -- screenshots.sh wipes its output dir, so the scene never runs
# with -o pointed at the assets. Run after readme-tour.scene.

note a colour platform opens straight to the duration picker; make a timer
press select        # off hours
press up 25         # twenty-five minutes
press select        # off minutes
press select        # confirm -- detail opens
press back          # menu, cursor on the timer row
press down          # to the cog row
press select        # Settings
press down 3        # to the Color row, which is last
press select        # the colour picker, opening on Picton Blue
shot color-picker
press down 3        # to Brilliant Rose
press select        # applies and pops back to settings
shot color-chosen
press back          # the recoloured list
shot color-list
